[01:25.52] Shine, shine, the light of good works shine
[01:35.93] The watch before the city gates, depicted in their prime
[01:45.08] The golden light all grimy now
[01:51.35] 300 years have passed
[01:53.64] The worthy Captain and his squad of troopers standing fast
[01:59.39] 
[02:07.40] The artist knew their faces well
[02:10.49] The husbands of his lady friends
[02:12.32] His creditors and councillors
[02:14.68] In armour bright, the merchant men
[02:16.55] Official moments of the guild
[02:18.63] In poses keen from bygone days
[02:20.61] City fathers frozen there
[02:22.52] Upon the canvas dark with age
[02:31.99] The smell of paint, a flask of wine
[02:34.87] And turn those faces all to me
[02:36.96] The blunderbuss and halberd-shaft
[02:39.04] The Dutch respectability
[02:40.92] They make their entrance one by one
[02:43.05] Defenders of that way of life
[02:45.10] The redbrick home, the bourgeoisie
[02:47.38] Guitar lessons for the wife
[02:50.98] 
[03:36.26] So many years we suffered here
[03:39.58] Our country racked with Spanish wars
[03:41.44] Now comes a chance to find ourselves
[03:43.48] Quiet reigns behind our doors
[03:45.52] Think about posterity again
[03:48.82] 
[04:18.45] So the pride of little men
[04:24.36] The burghers good and true
[04:26.81] Still living through the painter's hand
[04:29.35] Request you all to understand
[04:36.05] 